{
  "note": [
    "THE IDENTITY TEMPLATE, pinned.",
    "",
    "An allocation on the COPY DESK \u2014 one trader, one dollar amount \u2014 becomes a",
    "runnable strategy through exactly one function, and that function exists",
    "TWICE: `identity_strat` in api/src/copy.rs (which the live engine and the",
    "/copy API use) and `identityStrat` in app/lib/identityStrat.ts (which the",
    "browser and the backtest worker use). Two implementations of one template is",
    "how a backtest card ends up promising something the live session doesn't do.",
    "",
    "Each case below is an allocation and the strat it MUST produce. Both",
    "languages assert against this file, so a default changed on one side and not",
    "the other fails the build instead of quietly costing money. Numbers compare",
    "numerically (1 == 1.0); everything else is exact.",
    "",
    "Adding a knob to the template means adding it here first.",
    "",
    "`tradeFilters` is present ONLY when the allocation carries one: both halves omit the key otherwise, and this comparison is exact."
  ],
